## 5. Role and permission matrices

### 5.1 Platform roles & actions — `lib/rbac.ts`

| Role | Rank |
|---|---:|
| owner | 60 |
| admin | 50 |
| manager | 40 |
| staff | 30 |
| viewer | 20 |
| guest | 10 |

| Action | Min role |
|---|---|
| `admin:access` | viewer |
| `admin:manage` | admin |
| `portal:read` | guest |
| `portal:write` | staff |
| `org:manage` | admin |
| `billing:manage` | owner |

### 5.2 Gate matrix (@ `545c6251`)

| gate | mechanism | applies to |
|---|---|---|
| Portal middleware | `createSlugPortalMiddleware` + portal cookie/session; login `/portal/login` | `/portal/:slug*` except public auth paths |
| Portal page module gate | `requirePortalModule(slug, moduleId)` | each portal page |
| Portal API | `guardPortalApi` / `guardPortalApiCookie` → `requirePortalSession*` | `/api/portal/*` |
| Portal org check | `hasRequiredOrganization` — production non-placeholder `orgId` | portal sessions |
| Demo slugs | `demo-client`, `demo-website` special entitlements | demo |
| Admin middleware | HMAC `ea_admin_session` + `can(role, 'admin:access')` | `/admin/*` except public auth |
| Launch middleware | same admin cookie + `admin:access` | `/launch` |
| Admin pages | often double-check `verifyAdminSession` | e.g. master, factory |
| Admin API | `requireAdminSessionFromRequest` | `/api/admin/*` |

**Not present at SHA:** portal `LegalReacceptanceShell` gate; `redirectCtpClientFromExecutiveSurface` / `lib/ctp-executive-surface-redirect.ts` (executive dual surfaces remain fully reachable for CX clients).

**Roles in practice:** portal client (HMAC slug session), demo client, admin (platform roles via cookie). CTP is module + submission detection, not a separate RBAC role.

